    "description": "The objective of the Student Engagement Portal is to build an automated, camera-based system that observes a classroom during a live session and continuously estimates how attentive students are, without requiring any manual observation by the instructor. The system should translate raw visual behaviour — posture, gaze proxy, hand movement, and interaction cues — into a quantitative engagement score per student and for the class as a whole, and should present this information through a live dashboard as well as exportable reports (CSV and PDF) that a professor can review after the lecture. Specifically, the system aims to: • Detect and track every visible student in a classroom video feed using pose estimation, without requiring facial recognition or identity data. • Classify each tracked student's behaviour, frame-by-frame, into a small set of pedagogically meaningful states: focused, interacting with teacher, using phone, and drowsy / slouching. • Aggregate this frame-level telemetry into second-by-second and session-level engagement scores. • Surface class-wide and individual-level analytics through a REST API and web dashboard in real time. • Auto-generate a professional PDF audit report with pedagogical recommendations that an instructor can act on. Locally Hosted",
