    "summary": "QP Analyzer is an AI-powered system that automatically evaluates university question papers against course syllabi and previous-year papers. It assesses Bloom’s Taxonomy, syllabus coverage, difficulty, OBE/CO alignment, and question repetition to support academic quality assurance and accreditation compliance.",
    "description": "QP Analyzer converts the manual and subjective process of question-paper auditing into an automated, evidence-based workflow. Users can upload the course syllabus, examination paper, and previous-year question papers in PDF/DOCX format. The system performs document parsing and Vision OCR using Qwen2-VL-7B, followed by parallel AI-based question structuring using Qwen2.5-32B.\n\nThe multi-stage audit engine evaluates:\n* Bloom’s Taxonomy and cognitive-level distribution\n* Syllabus and unit-wise coverage\n* Easy/Moderate/Hard difficulty classification and Weighted Difficulty Index (WDI)\n* Outcome-Based Education (OBE) / Course Outcome mapping\n* Final moderation verdict and revision recommendations\n\nCore Problems Solved: \n● Manual Academic Auditing: Translates time-consuming, subjective manual quality reviews of exam \npapers into objective, data-driven evaluations. \n● Accreditation Compliance: Verifies that exams align with institutional Course Outcomes (COs) to \nsupport academic accreditation. \n● Cognitive Rigor Alignment: Evaluates papers against Bloom's Taxonomy cognitive levels to prevent \nexams from over-indexing on simple memory recall or being disproportionately difficult. \n● Curriculum Drift: Detects units or topics within the syllabus that are either omitted from the exams or \nexcessively tested. \n● Past Paper Repetition: Flags instances where questions from previous years are recycled directly, \nviolating institutional test integrity standards.\n\nResults are presented through an interactive React dashboard with charts, scores, recommendations, and downloadable PDF reports. The architecture uses local vLLM inference and SQLite-based response caching for efficiency. (Accessible via CSJM Secure Wi-Fi Network only)",
